      "side": 1,
      "message": "After some experiments, I think I can remove the Thread.sleep() in tearDown since the 45 seconds hang don\u0027t appear anymore. However, I could not find that their announcement of the fix in their patch note.\n\n(https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/test#core-1.6.0-alpha05, read from 1.5.0 which was released Nov 2022).\n\nAnyway, this can be removed since it seems not happening anymore.\n\n-----\n\nAbout this new `Thread.sleep()`, then it might not be related to b/159805732. I should fix the comment. Also, the workarounds in that bug is not applicable since b/159805732 is related to  closing the activity. \n\nWe may need some other way to remove/reduce the flakiness.\n\nHowever, one question is - is it really worth to spend time to investigate what\u0027s happening in ActivityScenario and find the other workaround, when we have already have a working workaround?",
